{
  "dom_id": "step-q61300",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "If $\\,\\boxed{}\\times 25%=90,$ then what is the missing number?",
  "worked_solution": "The part is $90,$ the percentage is $25%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\n \n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $25%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{100}=\\frac{25÷25}{100÷25}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =90÷25% \\\\  & =90÷\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =90\\times \\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =90\\times 4 \\\\  & =360\\end{aligned}\n$$",
